            "question": "Which of the following is NOT a distinctive characteristic of a typical cervical vertebra?",
            "options": [
              {
                "key": "A",
                "text": "The body is small and wider from side to side than anteroposteriorly."
              },
              {
                "key": "B",
                "text": "The vertebral foramen is large and triangular."
              },
              {
                "key": "C",
                "text": "The transverse processes contain transverse foramina."
              },
              {
                "key": "D",
                "text": "The articular processes contain superior facets directed inferoanteriorly."
              },
              {
                "key": "E",
                "text": "The spinous processes are short and bifid."
              }
            ],
            "answer": "D",
            "explanation": "The articular processes contain superior facets directed superoposteriorly (Moore, p 439).",
