            "question": "Which of the following is NOT a distinctive characteristic of a typical thoracic vertebra?",
            "options": [
              {
                "key": "A",
                "text": "The body is heart-shaped."
              },
              {
                "key": "B",
                "text": "The vertebral foramen is triangular and larger than in cervical and lumbar vertebrae."
              },
              {
                "key": "C",
                "text": "The transverse processes are long and strong and extend posterolaterally."
              },
              {
                "key": "D",
                "text": "The articular processes contain superior facets directed posteriorly and slightly laterally."
              },
              {
                "key": "E",
                "text": "The spinous processes are long and slope posteroinferiorly."
              }
            ],
            "answer": "B",
            "explanation": "The vertebral foramen is circular and smaller than the foramina of cervical and lumbar vertebrae (Moore, p 441).",
